course: dictionary
lesson: 15021
title: Words about breathing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Respiratory is a long word, but its meaning is simple: it has to do with breathing. Look at the words around it for clues. «The nurse counted Sam's respiratory rate while he sat still.» Counting breaths is part of checking how someone breathes, so respiratory rate must mean how fast a person breathes.
explain: Respiratory often comes before another word, and the pair tells you the meaning. A respiratory system is the parts of the body we breathe with. A respiratory infection is an illness in those parts, like a cold or flu. «Ben had a respiratory infection, so he coughed all week.»
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in breathing. «The respiratory system takes in air» becomes «the breathing system takes in air», which still makes sense. If your swap works, you have found the meaning.
fact: Respiratory means to do with breathing.
fact: The respiratory system is made of the nose, mouth, windpipe (trachea), bronchi and lungs.
fact: The respiratory system takes in oxygen and gives out carbon dioxide.
fact: Respiratory illnesses include colds, flu, asthma and Covid.
fact: Useful phrases are respiratory system, respiratory infection, respiratory problems and respiratory rate.
exercise: «Smoke can cause respiratory problems.» What does respiratory mean here? | To do with seeing and hearing | To do with moving and running | To do with eating and drinking | *To do with breathing
exercise: The respiratory system takes in oxygen. What does it give out? | Warmth | *Carbon dioxide | Water | Sound
exercise: «The nurse counted Sam's respiratory rate.» What is a respiratory rate? | How much someone weighs | *How many breaths someone takes in a minute | How tall someone is | How fast someone runs
test: Which of these is a respiratory illness? | Toothache | Sunburn | *Asthma | Broken arm
test: Which of these is part of the respiratory system? | Ear | *Lungs | Knee | Elbow
exam: «Lily had a cold, which is a respiratory illness.» What does respiratory tell you about the cold? | *It affects the breathing system | It is a kind of food | It only happens in summer | It makes you taller
